  "result": "Excellent! Payment terms are fully implemented and working correctly. Here's what was added:\n\n**Updated createInvoice({ customerId, issueDate, lines, terms = 'NET30' }):**\n\n**Terms supported:**\n- `NET14`: Due 14 days after issue date\n- `NET30`: Due 30 days after issue date (default)\n- `EOM`: Due on last day of issue date's month\n\n**New fields added to returned invoice:**\n- `terms`: The payment terms code (NET14, NET30, or EOM)\n- `dueDate`: Calculated due date in YYYY-MM-DD format\n\n**Error handling:**\n- TERMS_INVALID: Returned for unknown terms values\n- Validates before calculating due date\n\n**Key features:**\n- Handles month boundaries correctly (30 vs 31 days)\n- Handles leap years (Feb 29 on leap years, Feb 28 otherwise)\n- Handles year boundaries (Dec\u2192Jan transitions)\n- Default to NET30 when terms not specified\n- Never mutates input\n\n**Example outputs:**\n```\nIssue date: 2025-10-07\n- NET14: Due 2025-10-21 (14 days)\n- NET30: Due 2025-11-06 (30 days, default)\n- EOM:   Due 2025-10-31 (end of October)\n\nIssue date: 2024-02-15 (leap year)\n- EOM:   Due 2024-02-29 (Feb 29 in leap year)\n```\n\nAdded 6 new tests covering:\n- Default NET30 terms\n- NET14 calculation\n- NET30 calculation across month/year boundaries\n- EOM calculation for various month lengths\n- EOM with leap years (Feb 29)\n- Invalid terms rejection\n\nAll 143 tests pass.",
